WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.085
Turn quality goals into measurable agreements.

00:00:03.085 --> 00:00:09.725
State the metric, workload, threshold and
observation interval, including how failures are
counted.

00:00:09.725 --> 00:00:13.480
Capacity needs an activity model, not just a user
total.

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:20.120
For other attributes, distinguish an outcome from a
prescribed technology and test the outcome that

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:22.333
stakeholders actually care about.

00:00:22.333 --> 00:00:26.326
Optimize the end-to-end flow, not isolated component
rates.

00:00:26.326 --> 00:00:32.486
In this simplified producer-consumer model,
throughput is limited by combined production or

00:00:32.486 --> 00:00:34.787
consumption, whichever is smaller.

00:00:34.787 --> 00:00:38.442
Balancing the stages can outperform equal
allocations.

00:00:38.442 --> 00:00:45.007
State the equal-cost assumption and remember that
full CPU utilization is still a capacity limit,

00:00:45.007 --> 00:00:46.835
with no practical headroom.
